  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1049 PM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge will start to break down and build west late\nweek as an upper level trough pushes into the Northeast. This will\nstart to bring a gradual cooldown Friday into the weekend. It will\nstill be on the hot side over the holiday weekend but highs \nshould fall back into the low to mid 90s. Highs will continue to \ncool into early next week into the upper 80s to lower 90s which is\ngetting a little closer to seasonal norms. As the ridge breaks \ndown rain chances will increase but overall forcing will be weak \nkeeping the chances low to medium mainly during the afternoons.",
